Description: UT-2026-0115 - 安全修复
 Interactively started su (stdin is a tty) now allocates its own
 pseudo-terminal by default, so the target session does not share the
 controlling terminal with the caller session. This prevents
 TIOCSTI/TIOCLINUX ioctl command injection by a process in the
 unprivileged session (kernel < 6.2 or dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti=1).
 The pty slave and proxy stdin handling is unchanged (upstream
 lib/pty-session.c already keeps the slave cooked and makes the
 proxy stdin raw), so line editing and tab completion keep working.
 Use -T/--no-pty to opt out. runuser keeps its historical behavior.
Origin: internal, UT-2026-0115; mechanism per upstream su(1) --pty
 (https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/pull/2685
  https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/2863ed62d77bb2bae5aecc2297236d440ad21c4d)
Bug: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2016-2779
Last-Update: 2026-08-21
---

Index: deepin-util-linux/login-utils/su-common.c
===================================================================
--- deepin-util-linux.orig/login-utils/su-common.c
+++ deepin-util-linux/login-utils/su-common.c
@@ -1240,6 +1240,16 @@ int su_main(int argc, char **argv, int m
 	if (request_same_session || !command || !su->pwd->pw_uid)
 		su->same_session = 1;
 
+	/* UT-2026-0115: interactively started su runs in its own
+	 * pseudo-terminal so that the target session does not share the
+	 * controlling terminal with the caller session. This prevents
+	 * TIOCSTI/TIOCLINUX ioctl command injection by a process running
+	 * in the unprivileged session (kernel < 6.2 without
+	 * dev.tty.legacy_tiocsti, see su(1) --pty); use -T/--no-pty to
+	 * opt out. runuser keeps its historical behavior. */
+	if (!su->runuser && su->isterm)
+		su->force_pty = 1;
+
 	/* initialize shell variable only if "-u <user>" not specified */
 	if (su->runuser_uopt) {
 		shell = NULL;
